    "basis": "A 35 mm bar tile with fine raised shield spirals, separate rim, two plates, two spoons, tankard handle/foam and hidden shelf ware. Independent 78000/26000 triangle meshes and 1024/512 bakes preserve relief, dish depressions and carving. Compare 768/384 compact maps, especially floor flecks and spiral colour boundaries."
  },
  "reviewNotes": "PDF page 8 and native front/back/top plus a 1000 px shield view inspected. Source: 399816 triangles, 19990884 bytes, height 49.6161 mm. Full-height centre ray reaches floor 24.705460 mm, normal Z=.993616; mount datum 17 mm. Floor normal squares X=.382406 and Y=.040238 confirm Y grain. Two spoon PCA directions: [-.969469,.245216,0] and [-.956332,-.292282,0]. The plates and tankard join above 43.55 mm, so their union is not used as one material mask. Source plate centres [-11.1,-7.2] and [-11.1,6.6] have floors at 43.896385 and 45.010799 mm. Tankard centre [-7.45,-.35] reaches sculpted foam 49.128532 mm; its radius 1.8 mm footprint spans Z48.7225..49.3427, below the 49.6161 mm lip. Shield circle fit from 72 radial source rays: centre Y=.319246, Z=33.330580, radius=7.627044 mm. Flat green background is near X=-17.145; raised spirals reach -17.465. Red is limited to X<-17.20 and radius 6.72; the gold rim occupies radii 6.72..7.8 including its rounded outer bevel. Native radial probes show the flat field at radius 6.681 mm and raised rim at 6.881 mm. Per-pixel green paint restores the whole shield before the red/gold masks, retaining carved plank normals and preventing colour interpolation across long faces. Reference MT1-044 separates added utensils/shield from common timber and projects packed geometry back to MT1-046. Three exposed fasteners measured; fourth covered by spoon. Inspect all sides/top and shield close-up, both tiers and texture candidates; compare dish/foam surfaces in render/LOD/shadow and validate actual material channels before publication.",
